attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `yciO`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.18 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The first fork is at `rnm`**, column 1, carried by 88% {S2.c1}. Then the `trp` genes, columns 2 to 7, [[tryptophan biosynthesis]], carried by 87 to 88% {S2.c2-7, Q}. A branch of 27 families runs through columns 1 to 27 in 10 to 12%, [[rRNA pseudouridine synthase and protease]] {S2.b1}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.18 against 0.54 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 26, a fork column, 1.26 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 76 to 79, `cvrA` to `ycgB`, are carried by 43 to 35% of chromosomes {S2.c76-79}. The last column is `ycgB`, in 35% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 90% of genes**, 0.53 bits on average, perplexity 1.7 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.78 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 65% against 96% {C}.

